<title>UK: M&amp;A boom in Europe continued in H1 1997 - report.</title>
<headline>M&amp;A boom in Europe continued in H1 1997 - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The boom in European cross border mergers and acquisitions continued in the first six months of 1997, according to a report published on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Figures from Acquisitions Monthly magazine showed 1,051 cross-border acquisitions of companies based in the European Union worth 28.8 bllion pounds were recorded in the first half.</p>
<p>In the same period last year, the figure was 982 deals totalling 27 billion pounds.</p>
<p>U.S. companies continue to top the league table of acquirors with 305 deals worth 11.4 billion pounds, up from 202 deals worth 6.3 billion pounds a year ago.</p>
<p>A significant proportion of recent U.S. acquisitions was the result of interest in UK utilities.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
